 "Ānūka.--Geldner thinks that in its solitary occurrence in the Rigveda this word means an ornament. Roth takes it adverbially, and so do Ludwig and Oldenberg.\nFoot notes Vedische Studien, 3, 94.\nv. 33, 9.\nSt. Petersburg Dictionary. s.v.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["aanooka", "aanuuka", "ānūka", "ఆనూక", "ಆನೂಕ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["aanooka", "aanuuka", "ānūka", "ఆనూక", "ಆನೂಕ"]}], "anuraDas": [{"id": "anUrADAs", "headword": "अनूराधास्", "headword_slp1": "anUrADAs", "fold": "anuraDas", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "15. Anūrādhās or anurādhā, ‘propitious,’ is , and (perhaps also ) Scorpionis.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["anooraadhaa", "anooraadhaas", "anooraadhaas_15", "anuuraadhaa", "anuuraadhaas", "anuuraadhaas_15", "anūrādhā", "anūrādhās", "anūrādhās_15", "अनूराधा", "अनूराधास्", "అనూరాధా", "అనూరాధాస్", "అనూరాధాస్_౧౫", "ಅನೂರಾಧಾ", "ಅನೂರಾಧಾಸ್", "ಅನೂರಾಧಾಸ್_೧೫"], "synonyms_slp1": ["anooraadhaa", "anooraadhaas", "anooraadhaas_15", "anuuraadhaa", "anuuraadhaas", "anuuraadhaas_15", "anūrādhā", "anūrādhās", "anūrādhās_15", "anUrADA", "anUrADAs", "అనూరాధా", "అనూరాధాస్", "అనూరాధాస్_౧౫", "ಅನೂರಾಧಾ", "ಅನೂರಾಧಾಸ್", "ಅನೂರಾಧಾಸ್_೧೫"]}]}